  "about": "A small human-curated yardstick for the piece-based notice score. Each entry is one work a curator rated by eye on the five piece attributes, with a holistic notice label (high, medium, low). The notice score is measured against those labels; the rubric is not shown to the vision model.",
  "attributes": {
    "composition": "Structure and balance of the arrangement, 0..100.",
    "colorLight": "Handling of color and light, 0..100.",
    "subject": "Strength and interest of the subject, 0..100.",
    "originality": "Distinctiveness against the artist's known motifs, 0..100.",
    "condition": "Apparent physical condition, 0..100."
  },
  "notice_thresholds": { "high": 70, "medium": 45 },
  "provenance": "Curator pass over catalogued works with a stable visual record; each entry cites the review session. Labels are holistic judgments, not the weighted average, so they occasionally disagree with the score.",
  "limitations": "This is a small convenience sample, not an independent validation set. The attributes and the human labels often come from the same visual read and the same curator, so agreement is a sanity check on the score, not proof of quality. Genre and era are not balanced and the sample is too small to measure bias by genre or era; treat agreement as indicative only and revisit as the rubric grows.",
